A||||5||loafer87gt||Surging V6problems, stalls on idle.. help please||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||03-29-2000||12:07 AM||||Well guys, something is seriously wrong with my GT. It stalls on startup, and if you keep it the pedal to the floor the idles surges badly (eg. 3000 RPM, 0, 3000 ,0, 5000, 0 ,2000, 0)I just had GM do over $800 worth of work trying to figure out what was up with my GT. They replaced the distrubtor, cap and rotor, plugwires, & did the sparkplugs, and the car still wouldn't run worth a darn. I took it back to them and they then said that it was a faulty ignition module, paid for that and it ran good for about 50 kilometers and then started to act up again. I took it in again and told them that I'm getting really pissed at them and told them that it must be something computer related, and to check the codes. The mechanic said he did check the codes and it read that the MAP sensor code was triggered but he said that it was not a current code and to ignore it. I called them this morning and told them about Ogres post regarding the MAP sensor being as I had just washed my engine about a week ago, and they said they tested it and it is putting out the right voltage. They also stated that my EGR valve isn't functioning properly but that wouldn't cause the problem. The took the car out for two test drives, it died the first time, but ran fine the second time. So they told me the problem seem to have fixed itself (whatever). The thing that pissed me off is that they still demanded that I pay them for the labor and diagnostics, even though they did nothing! After picking it up for the dealership, the car died on me on the ride home. Soooo...  call the towing company for the 3rd time and back to the dealership. Now they are saying that my main ECM is shot and needs to be replaced. This will be another $250 plus labour and taxes. I don't know whether to go tell them to screw themselves or to tell them to order the part. I am so frustrated with these guys, but they are the only GM dealership in the city who are willing to work on a Fiero, and it is the same place where my car came from new, so I expect good service from them. So, if anyone has any ideas on what to do, whether it sounds like it is an ECM problem or any other suggestions, please get back to me.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||03-29-2000||12:18 AM||||  That's a dealer for ya! They have to be the biggest vulchers around. I'm sure if you problem is the ECM, that there are those on the Forum that can tell you  how you can do it yourself ans save$$$. Unfortunately I have not had that kind of experience to help you through it; or mabey that's fortunate...Idon't know. But I do know that help will be here soon.<P> Keep the FAITH!!<BR> BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||03-29-2000||08:03 PM||||Did they replace the ignition coil anywhere along the way?  Its been my experience that when the ignition module goes bad, the coil goes with it.  If I were you, I'd take it elsewhere to get a second opinion.  Car dealer repair shops pay some of the lowest wages to their mechanics.  They get them right out of school, and only keep them for short periods of time, only to replace them with more cheap "newbees".  They are inexperienced, and a lot of diagnosis is experience, just not a computer.  Ask some of your buds and co-workers, and try to find a well respected place.  It sounds like a problem that a good mechanic would be able to easily troubleshoot.  Good luck!  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||03-29-2000||09:34 PM||||The way it acts up, runs fine, acts up make sure there isn't a short/loose wire behind your fuse box. Play with it back and forth when she acts up again and see if it makes a difference. When I lost power in my GT I took mine to the dealer figuring they would know whats wrong......BIG MISTAKE! They told me #1 3 5 cylinders were so low in compression that I need a new engine. Depressed that I couldn't afford that, on the way home my foot hit the fuse box and VAROOOOM away I went. So I paid the dealer $87.00 to tell me I need a new engine when the whole time a TBI fuse wire was loose behind the box! Good luck loafer and don't give up just cause the dealer can't find the prob. I'll NEVER go back there again!||||reg||2
Z||000004||pollock||03-31-2000||01:45 PM||||I know after all the ignition work, this will sound highly unlikely to you, but clean out the throttle body.  Every time i've recommended this to anyone with any surging idle problems, it has fixed it.  There are cleaners available that are specifically intended for throttle bodies.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||03-31-2000||08:45 PM||||A similiar problem with my '87 GT.  Code 32: EGR.  I'm going to replace the EGR tube, the EGR valve was replaced last year.  A pain in the butt job. I'm having Mr. Goodwrench do it, $hutter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">.  Only four bolts to replace, but two are a pain to get to.||||reg||9
